# Certified Concealed — E-Book Rewriting Project

You are helping rewrite "Know Your Ammo: The Complete Self-Defense Ammunition Guide" (280 pages) into 100% original content for the "Certified Concealed" brand.

## CRITICAL: Read RULES.md First

Before doing ANY work on this project, read the file `RULES.md` in the project root. It contains all rewriting rules, formatting specifications, and legal compliance requirements. Follow them exactly.

## Project Structure

```
source-text/         ← Original PDF content extracted to chapter files
chapters/            ← YOUR OUTPUT — rewritten chapters go here  
output/              ← Generated .docx files
generate.js          ← Node.js script for .docx generation
RULES.md             ← Master rules document (READ THIS FIRST)
```

## Workflow

1. User says "rewrite chapter X" → Read `source-text/chapter_XX.md`
2. Read `RULES.md` to refresh on all rules
3. Rewrite the chapter following ALL rules (100% original language, no author names, neutral products)
4. Save to `chapters/chapter_XX.md`
5. When user asks to generate a .docx → use `generate.js` as template

## Key Rules Summary (full details in RULES.md)

- **100% original language** — every sentence rewritten, restructured paragraphs, different vocabulary
- **No author names** — remove all, replace with generic references
- **Neutral product mentions** — brands as educational examples only, no endorsements
- **Georgia font** throughout — sizes: Ch# 11pt, Title 15pt, Headings 15pt, Body 12pt
- **US Letter** 8.5x11, 1" margins, 1.5 line spacing
- **Key Takeaway boxes** — 1-2 per chapter, bold italic, grey left border
- **Image placeholders** — 2-4 per chapter, detailed descriptive text in brackets
- **Each chapter** gets: number, title, image, opening paragraphs, sections with headings, takeaway boxes

## Content Quality Standards

- Read the ENTIRE source chapter before writing anything
- Restructure the flow — change section order, split/combine sections
- Write from knowledge, not by paraphrasing
- Add technical depth where the source is thin
- Maintain factual accuracy (ballistic data, physics, dimensions)
- Tone: authoritative instructor speaking to serious carriers

## When Generating .docx Files

- Use the `docx` npm package (already installed)
- Follow the formatting spec in RULES.md exactly
- Validate output: the file should open cleanly in Word and Google Docs
- Use `generate.js` as your template — it has all paragraph builders pre-configured

## File Naming

- Source chapters: `source-text/chapter_01.md`, `chapter_02.md`, etc.
- Rewritten chapters: `chapters/chapter_01.md`, `chapters/chapter_02.md`, etc.
- Output docs: `output/KnowYourAmmo_Part1.docx`, `Part2.docx`, etc.
